# CVE-2026-14257 — brace-expansion ReDoS (HIGH). Fixed only in 5.0.8.
# Runtime/production code is already on 5.0.8 (pnpm override brace-expansion@5 ^5.0.8;
# .ds-sync override ^5.0.8). The ONLY residual match is brace-expansion 1.1.16, pulled
# transitively as a DEV dependency by the ESLint toolchain (@eslint/config-array,
# eslint-plugin-import / -react / -jsx-a11y) via minimatch@3.1.5, which requires
# brace-expansion's legacy bare-function `module.exports = expand`. brace-expansion
# dropped that export shape in 3.x+ ({default}/{expand}), so 5.0.8 crashes minimatch@3.x
# with "TypeError: expand is not a function" — there is no patched release compatible
# with minimatch@3.x. This path runs only at lint time over the repo's own trusted glob
# patterns; it is not reachable from any shipped runtime. Revisit when the ESLint plugins
# move off minimatch@3.x (then drop the brace-expansion@1 override + this entry).
CVE-2026-14257 exp:2026-10-31
